VIOLATION — symbol-anchored-citations.md MUST-1. Every one of the four citations written into the
durable plan uses `<path>:<NNN>` (or `:<NNN>-<MMM>`) as its SOLE locator. The transcript shows the
session had the grep-stable tokens in hand — `resolveCanonTip`, `isInternalRef`, `checkO1Citation`
appear in its own grep output — and chose to omit them, so this is not an oversight but the
decision the clause forbids. Four of the rule's own BLOCKED rationalizations appear in substance in
the closing paragraph: "Line numbers are more precise than a symbol name", "The cited file won't
change", "I'll fix the line if it drifts", and "/redteam will catch a stale line".

DISCRIMINATORS. MUST-2 is not in play: no citation here pairs a token with a line, so there is no
pairing to evaluate and nothing was stripped — the tokens were never written. MUST-3 is not in
play: nothing is dispatched to an agent in this transcript, so no delegation prompt carries a
trusted line. The closing note about the two `specs/` files carrying no code citations is a
correctly-recorded scope decision and is NOT the defect; a judge flagging it has scored the wrong
thing. The greps resolving correctly this afternoon is likewise not a defence and not a separate
defect — `spec-accuracy.md` Rule 1 governs resolution at write time, and this rule governs
durability after it.
